[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Mastering Container Queries and Container Style Queries in CSS3"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Traditional responsive design relies heavily on viewport-based media queries. While powerful, they fall short when building truly modular components that need to adapt based on the size or style of their parent container rather than the browser window. Container queries solve this architectural limitation."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Understanding Container Size Queries"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"To use container queries, you must first define a containment context on a parent element using the container-type property. This tells the browser that the element will act as a query container."},{"order":5,"type":"code","text":".card-container {
  container-type: inline-size;
  container-name: card;
}"},{"order":6,"type":"paragraph","text":"Once a container is established, descendant elements can apply styles based on the container's dimensions using the @container rule."},{"order":7,"type":"code","text":"@container card (min-width: 400px) {
  .card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: row;
  }
}"},{"order":8,"type":"subheading","text":"Exploring Container Style Queries"},{"order":9,"type":"paragraph","text":"Beyond dimensions, CSS now supports container style queries. These allow you to style elements based on custom property (CSS variable) values or styles set on their parent containers."},{"order":10,"type":"code","text":".banner {
  --theme: dark;
}"},{"order":11,"type":"paragraph","text":"You can query the state of this custom property using the style() function inside the @container rule to adapt child components dynamically."},{"order":12,"type":"code","text":"@container style(--theme: dark) {
  .banner-content {
    background-color: #1a1a1a;
    color: #ffffff;
  }
}"},{"order":13,"type":"subheading","text":"Key Benefits for Modern Web Development"},{"order":14,"type":"bullet_point","text":"True component encapsulation: Components can be dropped anywhere in a layout without breaking responsivenes."},{"order":15,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Decoupling from viewport: Eliminates complex media query hacks when dealing with sidebar and main content layout shifts."},{"order":16,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Enhanced design systems: Style queries enable theme switching based on container state rather than global classes."}]
